# The kernel's review (roadmap os-server.md P15), finding 3: spaces past SPACE_MAX (128 in all) are KE_POOL, and the
# kernel's data past the list of spaces stays whole (before: no limit, and
# the 129th space was written over the list's length). tests/programs/
# additions.asm, TEST_RV_SPACES; Bochs, whose timing the races need.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_RV_SPACES
emulators: bochs
match: contains
timeout: 60
---
additions: spaces made by the program (KE_POOL due at 128 in all): 115
additions: all of them deleted: 0
additions: an endpoint retyped after: 0
additions: done
